## Reflection

This project expanded my understanding of finite state machines by introducing transitions based on input signals rather than following a fixed sequence.

Unlike the traffic light controller, the elevator controller reacts to events such as a call button or arriving at a floor. This made the FSM more realistic and demonstrated how control logic is commonly implemented in digital systems.

## Problems

No major problems occurred during this project.

The main challenge was organizing the states and making sure every possible transition was handled correctly. Drawing the state diagram before coding made the implementation much easier.

